    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0661" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg495"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Swenson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 220</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-10-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your No. 128, of the 10th ultimo, transmitting copy of a new draft of
                    treaty for the proposed cession of the Danish West Indies to the United States,
                    embodying the accepted suggestions made in the note from the Danish Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs, of June 29, last, a copy of which was communicated to the
                    Department in my No. 212, dated Norseland, Minnesota, August 8, 1901.</p>
                <p>A copy of the amended project has been handed to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurits S. Swenson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
